====== Google Wifi ======

/* This template is intended to be used via https://openwrt.org/meta/create_new_device_page . */

Google Wifi is a 2x2 802.11ac AP with a quad-core Qualcomm IPQ4019 SoC, 512 MB RAM, and 4 GB eMMC storage. Its stock firmware is based on ChromeOS, including a bootloader based on [[https://coreboot.org/|Coreboot]] and [[https://libreboot.org/docs/depthcharge/|Depthcharge]], and can be convinced to run non-Google-signed software (such as OpenWrt) by entering Developer Mode.
The device is also known by its internal name "Google Wifi Gale"

There is also a model (GJ2CQ) without USB-C, using a DC barrel input (14V@1.1A) instead. Installation on the GJ2CQ requires soldering a USB port to four test points located on the PCB and using a screwdriver to short the unpopulated SW7 contacts at the appropriate time during installation. More information can be found in [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/google-wifi-no-usb/130774/15|this OpenWrt forum post]].

