===== Notes =====

Some technical references that may be useful:

  * [[https://github.com/marcosscriven/galeforce#how-to-apply-an-image|GaleForce]]: a past attempt at supporting custom software running on Google Wifi
    - Note that there is [[https://github.com/marcosscriven/galeforce/pull/47#issuecomment-660314698|some confusion]] about whether GaleForce still works on the latest Google software updates
    - [[https://github.com/marcosscriven/galeforce/commit/65428705d1baf5606d7bea04d2580415140ffdae]]

==== Upstreaming notes ====

A few features were provided by non-upstream kernel patches. Some development notes:

  * The factory bootloader does not yet reboot correctly when using upstream Linux drivers. See [[https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-msm/20200721080054.2803881-1-computersforpeace@gmail.com/|[RFC PATCH] firmware: qcom_scm: disable SDI at boot]] for description and initial patch. This likely needs resubmitted with a new Device Tree ''compatible'' property.
    * Merged to openwrt.git via [[commit>?p=openwrt/openwrt.git;a=commit;h=a93ec36630ef4ff5a2195ad613b616bffa50d00d|commit a93ec36630ef ("ipq40xx: qcom_scm: Disable SDI at boot")]]
  * The factory bootloader does not yet support SMP when using upstream Linux drivers. Instead, the device simply works with a single CPU. See [[https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-msm/20200913201608.GA3162100@bDebian/|[RFC] qcom_scm: IPQ4019 firmware does not support atomic API?]] for more info. This also may need a new ''compatible'' property and be submitted upstream.
    * Merged to openwrt.git via [[commit>?p=openwrt/openwrt.git;a=commit;h=26af098e0e97124a741c5c96a824b17e7f1b6434|commit 26af098e0e ("ipq40xx: qcom_scm: Fix cold boot address command")]]

